KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 8 --unwinding-assertions --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ ranges take: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Range-pipe over an array with std::views::take.  Two eras of failure:
originally a hard "conversion from 'signed int [5l]' to
'<<type:auto>>'" CONVERSION ERROR (silent all-templates deduction
failure, resolve with nargs=0, at forward@bind_back.h) -- that root
cause was the `= default` copy-constructor skeleton demanding a
DELETED default constructor of a base/member, fixed per N5008
[class.copy.ctor]/14 with the goto-symex family.  NOW the front end
recovers instead but SILENTLY DROPS the range-for loop and the
assertion from main() (wrong-code: goto-functions show arr/sum decls
then straight SET RETURN VALUE 0), so verification succeeds vacuously.
The desc requires the real assertion to be present and SUCCESS.

2026-09-24: the desc never passed `--stdlib libc++`, so it exercised the
libstdc++ headers -- where the same program (cpp20_ranges_basic) is CORE
now; the flag is added so this test is the libc++ variant it is tagged as.
Under libc++ 18 it still fails: `std::views::take(3)` is
`__range_adaptor_closure_t(std::__bind_back(*this, ...))`, and
`__bind_back`'s trailing `-> decltype(__bind_back_t<...>(...))` /
`__perfect_forward` chain is not resolved (the closure's type stays `auto`,
"function call expects function or function pointer as argument, but got
'<<type:auto>>'"; reduced: `std::__bind_back(fn{}, 3)` alone fails with an
enable_if_t<false> instantiation in <__compare/ordering.h>).
